Bob, I wholly agree, and I find usage in that sense quite annoying. My
idea is not so mch to spam down a list of words to stick behind "lo"
as it is to create a referential guide to conversation, which in turn
would (I hope) facilitate more conversation in lojban po'o. It has
been thorought burned into my mind that lujvo should be developed with
the intent to use it as a main selbri, and I thank my seniors in the
community for drilling that good habit into my thick skull. If
somebody would be so kind as to start sections on the wiki for this,
I'd be glad to start copying over terminology from jvs and generating
a request list of missing words. This also gives newnewnewnewbies
something constructive to do as they will probably have the most "how
do I say...?" questions, which means we get more material for the list.

